# API architecture

Follow `.agents/skills/elysiajs/SKILL.md`. Import via `@api/*`.

## Directories

| Dir | Owns | Must not |
|-----|------|----------|
| `interface/endpoint/` | HTTP routes, OpenAPI tags | Business rules, SQL |
| `interface/schema/` | Elysia `t` schemas + `Static<>` types | DB access |
| `interface/plugins/` | Auth macro, HTTP logger | Feature logic |
| `application/service/` | Use cases, DTO mapping, `AppException` | `status()`, route plugins |
| `domain/<feature>/` | Entities and domain rules | HTTP / `AppResponse` |
| `infrastructure/` | Config, logger, repositories (Drizzle) | HTTP shapes |
| `shared/` | Exceptions, Better Auth, `db`, utils | Feature orchestration |

## Routes

- Extend `apiRoute` (`/api/v1`, error handler, `authMacro`).
- One resource group: `apiRoute.group('/idiom', ...)`. Mix `auth: roleAdmin` and `auth: roleUser` per handler; do not split `/admin/...` paths.
- Handler: call a service, then `status(n, AppResponse.success(data).toJson())`.
- Declare `body` / `query` / `params` / `response` (including error statuses). Use `createSuccessResponseSchema` / `emptySuccessResponseSchema` / `errorResponseSchema`.
- Export `<resource>Tag` and register it in `app.ts` swagger `tags`. Mount the group in `index.ts` **before** `export type App` so Eden stays typed.
- Pagination: `paginationQuerySchema` + `paginationResponseSchema` from `schema/common.ts`.

```typescript
.post('', async ({ body, status }) => {
  const result = await createIdiom(body.text, body.meaning);
  return status(201, AppResponse.success(result).toJson());
}, {
  auth: roleAdmin,
  body: createIdiomBodySchema,
  response: {
    201: createSuccessResponseSchema(createIdiomResponseSchema),
    400: errorResponseSchema,
    409: errorResponseSchema,
    500: errorResponseSchema,
  },
  detail: { tags: [idiomTag.name], summary: 'Create an idiom' },
})
```

## Errors and logging

- Throw `AppException` subclasses (`NotFoundException`, `ConflictException`, …) with codes from `ERROR_CODES`.
- Add feature-specific codes next to the existing `IDIOM_*` entries.
- User-facing exception messages may be Chinese; OpenAPI `summary`/`description` stay English.
- Log with `@api/infrastructure/logger` (LogTape). Never `console.log`.
